      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:87:4",
      "text": [
        " مَنْ كَسَا مُؤْمِناً كَسَاهُ اللَّهُ مِنَ الثِّيَابِ الْخُضْرِ ",
        "وَ قَالَ فِي حَدِيثٍ آخَرَ لَا يَزَالُ فِي ضَمَانِ اللَّهِ مَا دَامَ عَلَيْهِ سِلْكٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Hammad Bin Isa, from Ibrahim Bin Umar, from Abu Hamza Al Sumaly, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Ali<sup class=\"bTxt\">asws</sup> Bin Al-Husayn<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The one who clothes a <span class=\"iTxt\">Momin</span>, Allah<sup>azwj</sup> would Clothe him from the green clothes’. ",
          "And he<sup>asws</sup> said in another Hadeeth: ‘He will not cease to be in the Guarantee of Allah<sup>azwj</sup> for as long as there is a fibre (from that cloth) upon him’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from Hammad ibn ‘Isa from Ibrahim ibn ‘Umar from abu Hamza al-Thumali from Ali ibn al-Husayn (a.s.) who has said the following: ’’Whoever provides clothes for a believer, for his reward Allah will dress him all in green.’ In another Hadith he said, ‘He will live under the protection of Allah as long as a fiber of that clothes is on him (believer).’” "
        ]
      }
    },
